[[:db/retract 17592186198696 :question/answer-fields 17592186194802] [:db/retract 17592186198727 :question/answer-fields 17592186195000] [:db/retract 17592186198727 :question/answer-fields 17592186195003] [:db/retract 17592186198727 :question/answer-fields 17592186194997] {:db/id 17592186198256 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2a099938-e369-51af-98a6-9db474374a4f" "question-389aeeff-ffb8-5897-88a3-b12029287eb6" "question-9889c22d-72d2-5a8b-9484-672aacb03351" "question-31bb631f-458f-5c01-a798-8fd4daa7d0e1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198113 :question/problem "$\\qquad$ $x$ is greater than $4,$ or $x$ is irrational.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is greater than $4$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is rational" :question/worked-solution "The sentence\n\n$\\qquad$ $x$ is irrational\n\ncan be expressed in symbolic form as $\\lnot Q.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\nP\\lor \\lnot Q.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198257 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-60b90c12-945a-57da-a90e-2ce25715910b" "question-501a9cd9-7487-5eca-998b-73598c18e09d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198105 :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\land B) = \\neg A \\lor \\neg B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is prime and $y$ divides $12$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is prime and }y\\text{ divides }12) & ≡¬(x\\text{ is prime}∧y\\text{ divides }12) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is prime})∨¬(y\\text{ divides }12) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not prime}∨y\\text{ does not divide }12 \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not prime}\\text{ or }y\\text{ does not divide }12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198258 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1f8070be-c520-5735-8b0d-89789f1b6296" "question-52356a50-945f-5f86-892e-4a577c3252b5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198114 :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg ( A \\lor B) = \\neg A \\land \\neg B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is a multiple of $5$ or $y$ divides $24$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is a multiple of [math]5[/math] or }y\\text{ divides }24) & ≡¬(x\\text{ is a multiple of }5∨y\\text{ divides }24) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is a multiple of }5)∧¬(y\\text{ divides }24) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not a multiple of }5∧y\\text{ does not divide }24 \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is not a multiple of }5\\text{ and }y\\text{ does not divide }24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a099938-e369-51af-98a6-9db474374a4f" :question/id #uuid "2a099938-e369-51af-98a6-9db474374a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183279" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is not a prime number, or $x$ is odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a prime number\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is an odd integer" :question/worked-solution "The sentence \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not a prime number.\n\n can be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\n¬P∨Q.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-26bb82e0-0c0d-55a3-bd34-42c77f1b96a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-26bb82e0-0c0d-55a3-bd34-42c77f1b96a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "26bb82e0-0c0d-55a3-bd34-42c77f1b96a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9d906c24-de54-5a30-9c80-33ff7dd0a5c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f18a6c49-0cde-515f-abf3-a29190e25c05" "answer-fe5d3bc9-21bf-5f26-aa13-aa7f00d9b808" "answer-5854f9fd-b31d-54b8-b452-73e06bd891b3" "answer-9d906c24-de54-5a30-9c80-33ff7dd0a5c4" "answer-66eaf105-5cf2-5632-b261-21e73c73f5b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f18a6c49-0cde-515f-abf3-a29190e25c05" :answer