73807ad-7593-517a-8539-d792e0490d5f" :answer/id #uuid "273807ad-7593-517a-8539-d792e0490d5f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a$ is even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a48b0346-6d35-51d5-a659-a0efe3f79d81" :answer/id #uuid "a48b0346-6d35-51d5-a659-a0efe3f79d81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a$ is odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c6da7b1-1d8f-5d5b-9c95-782705d288c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c6da7b1-1d8f-5d5b-9c95-782705d288c3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-d9a103b1-3885-5e01-9048-826ad395e098" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9a103b1-3885-5e01-9048-826ad395e098" "answer-4d10d194-f6ba-5aa0-a491-3f38890e07bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9a103b1-3885-5e01-9048-826ad395e098" :answer/id #uuid "d9a103b1-3885-5e01-9048-826ad395e098" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d10d194-f6ba-5aa0-a491-3f38890e07bc" :answer/id #uuid "4d10d194-f6ba-5aa0-a491-3f38890e07bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "or" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f9e3849-efb4-5220-9a4e-b78dd68376c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f9e3849-efb4-5220-9a4e-b78dd68376c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ca9bf587-4c7b-5f5c-9cfb-ee93ff22f238" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ca9bf587-4c7b-5f5c-9cfb-ee93ff22f238" "answer-33932fee-9b84-5ac2-80a4-e379807a1d82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca9bf587-4c7b-5f5c-9cfb-ee93ff22f238" :answer/id #uuid "ca9bf587-4c7b-5f5c-9cfb-ee93ff22f238" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$b$ is even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33932fee-9b84-5ac2-80a4-e379807a1d82" :answer/id #uuid "33932fee-9b84-5ac2-80a4-e379807a1d82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$b$ is odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199524 :tutorial/content "Logical operations with predicates generalize the corresponding operations on statements. As a result, all the properties of these operations are held.\n\nIn particular, for predicates $P(x_1,x_2\\ldots,x_n)$ and $Q(y_1,y_2\\ldots,y_m),$ De Morgan's laws state the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q) & ≡¬P∨¬Q \\\\ ¬(P∨Q) & ≡¬P∧¬Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese can be used to negate open sentences containing conjunctions and disjunctions. For example, let's negate the following:\n\n$$\nn \\ge 0 \\:\\textbf{ or }\\: 2 \\mid m\n$$\n\nApplying De Morgan's law for disjunctions, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(n\\ge 0\\,\\text{ or }\\,2∣m) & ≡¬(n\\ge 0∨2∣m) \\\\  & ≡¬(n\\ge 0)∧¬(2∣m) \\\\  & ≡n<0∧2∤m \\\\  & ≡n<0\\,\\text{ and }\\,2∤m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198518 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
